roducts-and-platforms/products/maps/all-together-now-group-planning-google-maps/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "product_strategy_resy_discover", "label": "Resy Discover", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 29, 197", "source_url": "https://blog.resy.com/newsroom/resy-launches-discover-tab/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "product_strategy_dice", "label": "DICE", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 30, 198", "source_url": "https://dicefm.zendesk.com/hc/en-gb/articles/22365422759313-Getting-started-with-DICE", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "product_strategy_simpleisure", "label": "Simpleisure", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 31, 199", "source_url": "https://simpleisure.com/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "product_strategy_scne", "label": "SCNE", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 32, 200", "source_url": "https://scne.ai/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "product_strategy_fluo", "label": "Fluo", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 33, 201", "source_url": "https://www.myfluo.com/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "product_strategy_group_fit_score", "label": "Group Fit Score", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 38-54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rank for the group rather than the loudest member or the creator, learning category/vibe, budget, travel tolerance, dietary and accessibility needs, timing habits, visit history and recent compromises, and explain each candidate succinctly."}, {"id": "product_strategy_constraint_aware_three", "label": "Constraint-Aware Three, Never a Feed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 56-64", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Natural language becomes structured constraints returning three credible choices; the anti-feed is the feature because the product reduces choice instead of manufacturing more browsing."}, {"id": "product_strategy_decision_protocol", "label": "Better Decision Protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 66-77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Private preference capture before totals, ranked or yes/okay/veto choices, deal-breakers separate from preferences, deterministic tie-breaking, an optional decide-for-us mode, fairness memory, and a deadline that actually closes server-side."}, {"id": "product_strategy_live_plan_resilience", "label": "Live Plan Resilience", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 79-88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The winner stays useful after the vote through availability and hours rechecks, travel and weather warnings, booking deep links, automatic fallback to option two, and reminders based on departure time rather than event time."}, {"id": "product_strategy_web_guests_native_regulars", "label": "Web Guests, Native Regulars", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 90-100", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The share link must stay excellent with no install or account so guests vote in seconds; the native app earns installation with saved groups, contacts/calendar, location, notifications and post-hangout memories."}, {"id": "product_strategy_memory_loop", "label": "The Memory Loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 102-111", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lightweight post-hangout feedback (went/skipped, worth repeating, actual spend, vibe accuracy, photos, attendance) feeds the next three options so the product compounds in value for a repeat group."}, {"id": "product_strategy_universal_hangout_model", "label": "Universal Hangout Model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 113-124", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Model format, energy, environment, commercial shape and context as independent dimensions; a padel court and a beach club differ operationally but share one canonical place/experience + availability + booking option + constraints model."}, {"id": "product_strategy_cross_platform_architecture", "label": "Cross-Platform Architecture", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 126-158", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Expo/React Native shares Supabase auth, generated types, domain rules, the decision engine, design tokens and analytics names, while navigation, notifications, contacts, calendar and location are built natively; shipping the Next.js UI in a webview does not count as native."}, {"id": "product_strategy_delivery_order", "label": "Recommended Delivery Order", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 160-169", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Secure auth and no-install share voting first, then taxonomy, constraint capture, Group Fit Score, booking handoffs, saved groups, native client, and only then fallback monitoring and payments."}, {"id": "product_strategy_anti_patterns", "label": "Strategy Anti-Patterns", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 171-180", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Avoid an infinite venue feed, shallow category sprawl, forcing voters to register, another group chat, an AI chatbot as the whole interface, unlabeled paid placement in the decision score, owning booking inventory early, and a social feed before repeat planning works."}, {"id": "product_strategy_revenue_paths", "label": "Trust-Preserving Revenue Paths", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 182-188", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Affiliate revenue only after the winner is decided, premium concierge, venue tools, clearly labeled sponsored candidates that never secretly alter ranking, and group payment facilitation when operationally ready."}], "edges": [{"source": "product_strategy_group_decision_layer", "target": "product_strategy_competitive_landscape", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "lines 5-34", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "product_strategy_competitive_landscape", "target": "product_strategy_partiful", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "line 20", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "product_strategy_competitive_landscape", "target": "product_strategy_apple_invites", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "line 21", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "product_strategy_competitive_landscape", "target": "product_strategy_howbout", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRODUCT